  "photography": {
    "Overview": "The first photographs of the entire Earth by satellites and crewed Apollo missions brought a new sense of Earth and promoted ideas of the unity of humanity. Photographs taken by explorers on the Moon evoked the experience of being in another world. The Pillars of Creation taken by the Hubble Space Telescope and other Hubble photos often evoke intense responses from viewers; for example, Hubble's planetary nebula images."
